; expect-error: E_TYPE_MISMATCH
; `try` catches a panic, not an Err, and the type checker is what stops you
; from pretending otherwise: the body yields a Result and the handler an Int,
; so the two branches cannot have one type. Handle an Err with `match`.
; (tests/regression/error-as-value.zyl covers the runtime halves.)
(defn main ()
  (print (try (error "x") (catch e 7))))
